      "SubmissionStatus": {
        "type": "string",
        "enum": [
          "graded",
          "excused",
          "submitted_ungraded",
          "missing",
          "not_due"
        ],
        "title": "SubmissionStatus",
        "description": "Why a grade is or is not a number.\n\n`EXCUSED` is the one that matters and the one most systems get wrong. An excused\nassignment leaves the denominator entirely — it is not a zero, and treating it as\none silently lowers a real child's real grade. It is a distinct member here so the\naggregation cannot collapse it by accident."
      },
